# AI Mini projects
- **TF-IDF Tokenizer (tf-idf.ipynb)**: Short explanation: toy implementation of a TF–IDF tokenizer (preprocess, TF, IDF, TF-IDF) and demo on sample documents. Tools/technologies used: Python (re, collections.Counter, math). Results/accuracy: no classification metrics — produces TF/IDF dictionaries and TF‑IDF scores.

- **Students Performance Regression (students_performance.ipynb)**: Short explanation: EDA, feature engineering, and regression models (LR, RF) to predict math score; feature selection and hyperparameter tuning. Tools/technologies used: pandas, numpy, seaborn, matplotlib, scipy, scikit-learn (LinearRegression, RandomForestRegressor, GridSearchCV), StandardScaler. Results/accuracy: Best reported — Linear Regression: Train MSE 29.4198, Test MSE 28.8911, Train R2 0.8695, Test R2 0.8813.

- **Temporal Difference — SARSA & Q-Learning (reinforcment_learning_temporal_difference.ipynb)**: Short explanation: discretised MountainCarContinuous adapter; tabular SARSA and Q‑learning agents; experiments sweeping α, ε, discretisation and comparing TD/MC/DP. Tools/technologies used: Python, numpy, gymnasium, matplotlib. Results/accuracy: reports learning metrics (avg last-100 returns, best episode rewards). Example outcomes: SARSA avg_last_100 ≈ 10.29 (best ep 43.15); Q‑Learning avg_last_100 ≈ 6.63 (best ep 43.25); convergence/stability analysis included.

- **MNIST with SVM (MNIST.ipynb)**: Short explanation: fetch MNIST, preprocess (normalizer), implement multiclass SVM via quadratic solver (cvxopt) and one-vs-rest training, tune C. Tools/technologies used: sklearn (fetch_openml), cvxopt, numpy, scikit-learn metrics. Results/accuracy: notebook computes and prints classification report and accuracy for chosen C (no single fixed number hard-coded).

- **MNIST — Different Models (MINIST_with_different_models.ipynb)**: Short explanation: compares ANN, SVM, and multiple CNN architectures/variants (epochs, LR, batch size, activations, optimizers, dropout) and recommends efficient model. Tools/technologies used: TensorFlow / Keras, sklearn, numpy, matplotlib. Results/accuracy: ANN ≈ 97.2–97.7% (varies with epochs); CNN variants: Opt-1 best raw test accuracy 99.15%, Opt-4 recommended tradeoff ≈ 98.90% (recommended 15 epochs → ~98.97% test in places).

- **Linear Regression with Gradient Descent (LinearRegression_with_GradiantDesent.ipynb)**: Short explanation: implements linear regression via gradient descent on synthetic data (make_regression), prints loss iterations and evaluates MSE. Tools/technologies used: numpy, sklearn.datasets, matplotlib. Results/accuracy: reports final MSE on test set (numeric MSE printed in notebook).

- **Iris — Gaussian Naive Bayes (iresData_with_GaussianNaiveBase.ipynb)**: Short explanation: load Iris, custom/train/test splits, train GaussianNB, evaluate, plot decision boundaries for two features. Tools/technologies used: pandas, numpy, matplotlib, scikit-learn (GaussianNB, cross_val_score). Results/accuracy: notebook prints training/test accuracy and 4‑fold CV mean (values computed by the code).

- **IMDB Sentiment Analysis (imdb-sentiment-analysis.ipynb)**: Short explanation: preprocess IMDB (padding), train and compare SimpleRNN, LSTM, GRU (with early stopping / checkpoints), evaluate and show classification reports. Tools/technologies used: TensorFlow / Keras (Embedding, RNN/LSTM/GRU), sklearn metrics. Results/accuracy: reported test accuracies ~ SimpleRNN 82%, LSTM 87%, GRU 87% (GRU/LSTM similar; GRU noted as preferred for simplicity).

- **FastText (fasttext.ipynb)**: Short explanation: preprocess Yelp tips, train a gensim FastText model, test pretrained fastText and update it with the corpus, inspect nearest/opposite words. Tools/technologies used: gensim FastText, NLTK, pandas. Results/accuracy: no classification metrics — shows word similarity/analogy outputs.

- **Brain Tumor Classification (brain-tumer-classification.ipynb)**: Short explanation: load MRI images, preprocess (background removal, CLAHE, blur), extract HOG features, PCA, train SVM (RBF) and evaluate. Tools/technologies used: OpenCV, scikit-image (HOG), scikit-learn (PCA, SVC), numpy, matplotlib. Results/accuracy: notebook prints training and test accuracy / classification report and confusion matrices (values produced when run).
